{
  "$comment": [
    "Compile-smoke manifest for every tests/haxe/**/*.hxml entry (task t-mwhjzgfh-l4pn).",
    "tests/haxe-compile-smoke.test.ts asserts that the set of entries here equals the set of .hxml files under tests/haxe/,",
    "so a new entry that is not listed fails the smoke; it is not skipped silently.",
    "mode=compile: `haxe <path> [defines]` must exit 0.",
    "mode=reject: it must exit non-zero AND combined output must contain `diagnostic` (a diagnosed rejection, not a crash).",
    "`targets` records which target compiler(s) the entry enables; it is documentation for reviewers, not used by the runner."
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "treeOutputDefines": true,
    "outPlaceholder": "<out>",
    "note": "For an entry whose text contains `<target>compiler.Compiler.use()`, the smoke appends -D <target>-output=<out>/gen and -D <target>-test-output=<out>/gen-tests, where <out> is the entry's scratch dir. This is the survey's proven invocation (output directory ... is not defined is a caller-parameter gap, not a defect). Per-entry `defines` are appended after the defaults."
  },
  "prepareDirs": [
    "out/haxe",
    "reference/haxe/gen",
    "reference/haxe/gen-tests",
    "reference/haxe-f32/gen",
    "reference/haxe-f32/gen-tests"
  ],
  "prepareDirsReason": "The generation step and compile.hxml write with -js into these directories; a fresh checkout has none of them (all are gitignored), and the entries must not depend on the smoke creating them implicitly.",
  "generateBundles": [
    "haxe",
    "haxe-f32"
  ],
  "generateReason": "test-main.hxml/test-main-f32.hxml compile -main TestMain against reference/haxe[-f32]/gen-tests, which is gitignored and absent on a fresh checkout; the smoke generates both trees from boring.json (the haxe bundles) before the pool starts, so it never races the tree it needs.",
